IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-art01-03`
IMPORT `epd-art04`
IMPORT `epd-art05-06`
IMPORT `epd-art07-08`
IMPORT `epd-art09-11`
IMPORT `epd-art12`
IMPORT `epd-art13`
IMPORT `epd-art14-21`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), Publications Office consolidated version of 19.12.2009 -- THE SEAT LAYER OF THE INDIVIDUAL.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who uses a publicly available electronic communications service as a subscriber, a user, or the recipient of a
-- message: one person, with one provider, one line or account, and one message at a time.
--
-- This layer phrases the layer-1 modules (epd-art01-03 ... epd-art14-21) as the questions that person asks. It restates no rule: every
-- question calls one layer-1 function with every argument named, from plain inputs (yes/no, a date, a choice from a list) worded as the
-- person is asked. The provider's seat (epd-seat-provider.l4) and the sender's seat (epd-seat-sender.l4) are separate layers over
-- the same modules, so the three seats cannot disagree about the law.
--
-- A DIRECTIVE BINDS MEMBER STATES, NOT PEOPLE. Where the text says "Member States shall ensure that I ...", the answer says what the
-- DIRECTIVE requires the national law to give or impose; it does not say what any one Member State's transposing law says, or whether a
-- provision has direct effect (NOTES.md).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. JUST TRUE = the text says yes. JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words. NOTHING = the text does not
-- answer (it is silent, limits itself, lists without closing, or points outside the sources). NOTHING is not "no" (NOTES.md,
-- "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
--
-- Borrowed terms (the data subject's consent, personal data, a publicly available electronic communications service, direct marketing,
-- and the other terms Article 2 takes from Directives 95/46/EC and 2002/21/EC) are facts the person states: the person says whether
-- the borrowed requirements are met.
--
-- The Marketing means and the national option are choices from a list (the layer-1 nouns module, epd-nouns).
-- The authorities' and the courts' powers appear only as what they mean for the person asking.

§ `ePrivacy Directive -- the individual's questions`

§§ `Is the Directive on this at all (Articles 1 to 3)?`

-- JUST FALSE = the Directive does not apply (Art 1(3) excludes it). NOTHING = Art 1(3) does not exclude it, which is not the same as saying the Directive applies (Art 3).
@export Does the Directive apply to this activity (Art 1(3))?
GIVEN `the activity is outside the Treaty on the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what is being done outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community (for example under Titles V or VI of the Treaty on European Union)?
      `the activity concerns public security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what is being done concern public security?
      `the activity concerns defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what is being done concern defence?
      `the activity concerns State security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what is being done concern State security?
      `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what is being done concern the economic well-being of the State?
      `the activity relates to State security matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what is being done relate to State security matters?
      `the activity is the State acting in criminal law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what is being done an activity of the State in areas of criminal law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive apply to what is being done` IS
    `Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` WITH
        `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS `the activity is outside the Treaty on the Community`
        `the activity concerns public security` IS `the activity concerns public security`
        `the activity concerns defence` IS `the activity concerns defence`
        `the activity concerns State security` IS `the activity concerns State security`
        `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State`
        `the activity relates to State security matters` IS `the activity relates to State security matters`
        `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS `the activity is the State acting in criminal law`

@export Does the Directive apply to the processing of my personal data (Art 3)?
GIVEN `the processing is of my personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what is being done a processing of your personal data?
      `the processing is for a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in connection with a publicly available electronic communications service (for example a phone, internet access or e-mail service offered to the public)?
      `the network is a public communications network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the network a public communications network (including a public network that supports data collection and identification devices)?
      `the network is in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the network in the Community (the European Union)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive apply to the processing of my personal data` IS
    `Art 3 the Directive applies to the processing` WITH
        `the processing is of personal data` IS `the processing is of my personal data`
        `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS `the processing is for a publicly available electronic communications service`
        `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices` IS `the network is a public communications network`
        `the network is in the Community` IS `the network is in the Community`

@export I am a company or other legal person: does the Directive protect my legitimate interests (Art 1(2))?
GIVEN `I am a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a legal person (a company or other organisation) rather than a natural person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a legal person do I have my legitimate interests protected by the Directive` IS
    `Art 1(2) the Directive provides for protection of the subscriber's legitimate interests` WITH
        `the subscriber is a legal person` IS `I am a legal person`

@export Am I a "user" under the Directive (Art 2(a))?
GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person?
      `I use a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use a publicly available electronic communications service, for private or business purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a user under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(a) the person is a user` WITH
        `the person is a natural person` IS `I am a natural person`
        `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service` IS `I use a publicly available electronic communications service`

@export Is what happened to my data a "personal data breach" (Art 2(i))?
GIVEN `there was a breach of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a breach of security?
      `my data was accidentally or unlawfully destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it lead to the accidental or unlawful destruction of your data?
      `my data was accidentally or unlawfully lost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it lead to the accidental or unlawful loss of your data?
      `my data was accidentally or unlawfully altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it lead to the accidental or unlawful alteration of your data?
      `my data was disclosed without authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it lead to unauthorised disclosure of your data?
      `my data was accessed without authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it lead to unauthorised access to your data?
      `the data was personal data held for a public communications service in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what happened to my data a personal data breach` IS
    `Art 2(i) the event is a personal data breach` WITH
        `the event is a breach of security` IS `there was a breach of security`
        `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data` IS `my data was accidentally or unlawfully destroyed`
        `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data` IS `my data was accidentally or unlawfully lost`
        `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data` IS `my data was accidentally or unlawfully altered`
        `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data` IS `my data was disclosed without authority`
        `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data` IS `my data was accessed without authority`
        `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community` IS `the data was personal data held for a public communications service in the Community`

@export Is this message "electronic mail" under the Directive (Art 2(h))?
GIVEN `it is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a text, voice, sound or image message?
      `it was sent over a public communications network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent over a public communications network?
      `it stays stored until I collect it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be stored in the network or on your device until you collect it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this message electronic mail under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(h) the message is electronic mail` WITH
        `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS `it is a text, voice, sound or image message`
        `the message is sent over a public communications network` IS `it was sent over a public communications network`
        `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient` IS `it stays stored until I collect it`

@export Is what I did "consent" under the Directive (Art 2(f))?
GIVEN `what I did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what you did count as the data subject's consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC (freely given, specific and informed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I did consent under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(f) the act of the user or subscriber is consent` WITH
        `the act of the user or subscriber is the data subject's consent in Directive 95/46/EC` IS `what I did is consent in the sense of Directive 95/46/EC`

§§ `My communications and my device (Article 5)`

@export Must my communications and the related traffic data be kept confidential (Art 5(1))?
GIVEN `it is my communication or traffic data about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it one of your communications, or traffic data about one?
      `it is by a public network or publicly available service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by means of a public communications network or a publicly available electronic communications service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my communications and traffic data be kept confidential` IS
    `Art 5(1) first sentence the Directive requires the confidentiality of the communication and the related traffic data` WITH
        `the thing is a communication, or traffic data related to a communication` IS `it is my communication or traffic data about it`
        `it is by means of a public communications network or a publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it is by a public network or publicly available service`

@export Must the Member State prohibit this person from listening to or intercepting my communications (Art 5(1))?
GIVEN `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance?
      `it is of my communications or related traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it of your communications or the related traffic data?
      `it is by someone other than a user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by someone other than a user of the communication?
      `I consented to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (the users concerned) consent?
      `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it legally authorised in accordance with Article 15(1) (a lawful restriction for national security, defence, public security or the investigation of crime)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must this interception of my communications be prohibited` IS
    `Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` WITH
        `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance`
        `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS `it is of my communications or related traffic data`
        `the act is by a person other than a user` IS `it is by someone other than a user`
        `the users concerned have consented` IS `I consented to it`
        `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)`

-- JUST FALSE = the paragraph does not prevent it ("shall not prevent").
@export Does the confidentiality rule stop my provider storing data that is technically needed to carry my communication (Art 5(1))?
GIVEN `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it technical storage which is necessary for conveying your communication?
      `the storage is without prejudice to confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the storage without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the confidentiality rule stop technical storage needed to carry my communication` IS
    `Art 5(1) third sentence the paragraph prevents the storage` WITH
        `the storage is technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication` IS `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance`
        `the storage is without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality` IS `the storage is without prejudice to confidentiality`

-- JUST FALSE = paragraph 1 does not affect it ("shall not affect").
@export Does the confidentiality rule stop a business recording my call as evidence of a transaction (Art 5(2))?
GIVEN `the recording is legally authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recording legally authorised?
      `the recording is of communications and related traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a recording of communications and the related traffic data?
      `the recording is in the course of lawful business practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it carried out in the course of lawful business practice?
      `the recording is to provide evidence of a business transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the confidentiality rule stop a business recording my call as evidence` IS
    `Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` WITH
        `the recording is legally authorised` IS `the recording is legally authorised`
        `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` IS `the recording is of communications and related traffic data`
        `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` IS `the recording is in the course of lawful business practice`
        `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication` IS `the recording is to provide evidence of a business transaction`

@export Is storing information on my device, or reading what is on it, allowed only with my consent (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `it is storing, or gaining access to, information in my device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the storing of information in your terminal equipment (your phone, computer or other device), or the gaining of access to information already stored there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is storing information on my device or reading it allowed only with my consent` IS
    `Art 5(3) first sentence the storing or access is only allowed on condition of consent` WITH
        `the act is the storing of information, or the gaining of access to information already stored, in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user` IS `it is storing, or gaining access to, information in my device`

@export Was the condition of consent met for what was stored on, or read from, my device (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `I gave consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your consent?
      `I was given clear and comprehensive information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given clear and comprehensive information, including about the purposes of the processing?
      `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the consent and the information in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the condition of consent met for what was stored on or read from my device` IS
    `Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` WITH
        `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS `I gave consent`
        `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS `I was given clear and comprehensive information`
        `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC`

-- JUST FALSE = the first sentence does not prevent it ("This shall not prevent").
@export Does the consent rule stop storing or access on my device that is strictly necessary for a service I asked for (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `it is technical storage or access` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it technical storage or access?
      `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network?
      `I explicitly asked the service provider for the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you explicitly ask the provider of the online service for that service?
      `it is strictly necessary for that provider to give me the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the storage or access strictly necessary for that provider to give you the service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the consent rule stop storage on my device strictly necessary for a service I asked for` IS
    `Art 5(3) second sentence the first sentence prevents the storage or access` WITH
        `it is technical storage or access` IS `it is technical storage or access`
        `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network` IS `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication`
        `the provider of an information society service was explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service` IS `I explicitly asked the service provider for the service`
        `the storage or access is strictly necessary in order for that provider to provide the service` IS `it is strictly necessary for that provider to give me the service`

§§ `My traffic data (Article 6)`

@export Must my provider now erase my traffic data or make it anonymous (Art 6(1))?
GIVEN `it is traffic data about me held by my provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it traffic data about you (the data processed to carry your communications), processed and stored by your provider?
      `my provider no longer needs it to carry my communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data no longer needed to carry the communication?
      `another rule lets my provider keep it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Art 6(2), (3) or (5), or Article 15(1), apply to the data (billing, your consent to marketing, the restriction of handling, or a lawful restriction)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my provider erase my traffic data or make it anonymous` IS
    `Art 6(1) the provider must erase the traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH
        `the data is traffic data relating to subscribers and users, processed and stored by the provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it is traffic data about me held by my provider`
        `the data is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication` IS `my provider no longer needs it to carry my communication`
        `paragraph 2, 3 or 5 of this Article or Article 15(1) applies to the data` IS `another rule lets my provider keep it`

@export May my provider still process my traffic data for billing on this date (Art 6(2))?
GIVEN `it is data needed for billing and interconnection payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data necessary for billing you and for interconnection payments?
      `the date of the processing` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the data being processed?
      `the last day my bill can be challenged or payment pursued` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my provider still process my traffic data for billing on this date` IS
    `Art 6(2) the processing of the traffic data for billing is permissible on the date` WITH
        `the data is necessary for the purposes of subscriber billing and interconnection payments` IS `it is data needed for billing and interconnection payments`
        `the date of the processing` IS `the date of the processing`
        `the last day of the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued` IS `the last day my bill can be challenged or payment pursued`

@export May my provider process my traffic data for marketing or value added services (Art 6(3))?
GIVEN `it is for marketing electronic communications services or for a value added service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose the marketing of electronic communications services, or the provision of a value added service?
      `I gave my prior consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your prior consent?
      `the processing goes no further than the services or marketing need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing only to the extent and for the duration necessary for those services or that marketing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my provider process my traffic data for marketing or value added services` IS
    `Art 6(3) first sentence the provider may process the traffic data` WITH
        `the purpose is marketing electronic communications services or the provision of value added services` IS `it is for marketing electronic communications services or for a value added service`
        `the subscriber or user to whom the data relate has given his or her prior consent` IS `I gave my prior consent`
        `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for such services or marketing` IS `the processing goes no further than the services or marketing need`

@export Can I withdraw my consent to the processing of my traffic data at any time (Art 6(3))?
GIVEN `my consent was for processing traffic data under Art 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your consent to the processing of your traffic data for marketing or value added services?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I withdraw my consent to the processing of my traffic data at any time` IS
    `Art 6(3) second sentence the user or subscriber has the possibility to withdraw the consent at any time` WITH
        `the consent was given for the processing of traffic data under paragraph 3` IS `my consent was for processing traffic data under Art 6(3)`

@export Has my provider told me what it must about my traffic data (Art 6(4))?
GIVEN `the processing is for marketing or a value added service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing for marketing electronic communications services or a value added service (which needs your consent)?
      `my provider told me the types of traffic data processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your provider tell you the types of traffic data it processes?
      `my provider told me how long it processes them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your provider tell you how long it processes them?
      `my provider told me before it asked for my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your provider tell you before it asked for your consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my provider told me what it must about my traffic data` IS
    `Art 6(4) the provider's duty to inform the subscriber or user is met` WITH
        `the purpose is the one mentioned in paragraph 3 (marketing, or value added services)` IS `the processing is for marketing or a value added service`
        `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed` IS `my provider told me the types of traffic data processed`
        `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the duration of such processing` IS `my provider told me how long it processes them`
        `the provider did so prior to obtaining consent` IS `my provider told me before it asked for my consent`

@export Is the handling of my traffic data restricted as Art 6(5) requires?
GIVEN `it is handled by someone under the authority of my provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data handled only by persons acting under the authority of your provider?
      `the handling is for one of the listed activities` IS A `Traffic data activity` @desc What is the handling for? One of: billing, traffic management, customer enquiries, fraud detection, marketing electronic communications services, providing a value added service, another activity.
      `the handling goes no further than the activity needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the handling restricted to what is necessary for that activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the handling of my traffic data restricted as Article 6(5) requires` IS
    `Art 6(5) the processing of the traffic data is restricted as required` WITH
        `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of a provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it is handled by someone under the authority of my provider`
        `activity` IS `the handling is for one of the listed activities`
        `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of such activities` IS `the handling goes no further than the activity needs`

§§ `A few more rights as the person called or located (Articles 7 and 9)`

@export I get itemised bills: must my privacy as a caller or called person be reconciled with that (Art 7(2))?
GIVEN `I receive itemised bills` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive itemised bills?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I get itemised bills: must the callers and called persons privacy be reconciled with that` IS
    `Art 7(2) the Member State must apply national provisions to reconcile the rights of subscribers receiving itemised bills with the privacy of calling users and called subscribers` WITH
        `the subscriber receives itemised bills` IS `I receive itemised bills`

@export Must my provider tell me before asking my consent to location processing (Art 9(1))?
GIVEN `my provider is asking for my consent to location processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your provider obtaining your consent to the processing of your location data (other than traffic data)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my provider tell me before asking my consent to location processing` IS
    `Art 9(1) second sentence the service provider must inform the users or subscribers before obtaining their consent` WITH
        `the provider is obtaining the consent of the users or subscribers to the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS `my provider is asking for my consent to location processing`

@export Once I have consented to location processing, must I be able to refuse it temporarily (Art 9(2))?
GIVEN `I consented to location processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to the processing of your location data other than traffic data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Once I have consented to location processing must I be able to refuse it temporarily` IS
    `Art 9(2) the user or subscriber must continue to have the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing` WITH
        `consent of the users or subscribers has been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS `I consented to location processing`

§§ `More of the Directive's own terms and my other rights (Articles 2, 8, 10, 12 and 16)`

@export Is this data "traffic data" under the Directive (Art 2(b))?
GIVEN `it is processed to convey a communication on a network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network?
      `it is processed for billing a communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data processed for the billing of a communication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this data traffic data under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(b) the data is traffic data` WITH
        `the data is processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network` IS `it is processed to convey a communication on a network`
        `the data is processed for the billing of a communication` IS `it is processed for billing a communication`

@export Is this data "location data" under the Directive (Art 2(c))?
GIVEN `it is processed in a network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data processed in an electronic communications network?
      `it is processed by a service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data processed by an electronic communications service?
      `it shows where my device is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the data indicate the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this data location data under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(c) the data is location data` WITH
        `the data is processed in an electronic communications network` IS `it is processed in a network`
        `the data is processed by an electronic communications service` IS `it is processed by a service`
        `the data indicates the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it shows where my device is`

@export Is what I exchanged a "communication" under the Directive (Art 2(d))?
GIVEN `it was exchanged between a finite number of parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties?
      `it went by a publicly available service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I exchanged a communication under the Directive` IS
    `Art 2(d) the information is a communication` WITH
        `the information is exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties` IS `it was exchanged between a finite number of parties`
        `the information is exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it went by a publicly available service`

@export Can I hide my number on every call from my line, not call by call (Art 8(1))?
GIVEN `I can prevent the presentation of my number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification?
      `I can do it for the whole line` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the possibility on a per-line basis?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I hide my number on every call from my line not call by call` IS
    `Art 8(1) second sentence the calling subscriber's possibility on a per-line basis is met` WITH
        `the calling subscriber has the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` IS `I can prevent the presentation of my number`
        `the possibility is on a per-line basis` IS `I can do it for the whole line`

@export Has my Member State ensured transparent procedures for overriding the hiding of my number (Art 10)?
GIVEN `there is a procedure governing how my provider may override` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a procedure governing the way in which the provider may override the elimination of calling line identification?
      `the procedure is transparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the procedure transparent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my Member State ensured transparent procedures for overriding the hiding of my number` IS
    `Art 10 the Member State has ensured transparent procedures governing the override` WITH
        `there is a procedure governing the way in which the provider may override` IS `there is a procedure governing how my provider may override`
        `the procedure is transparent` IS `the procedure is transparent`

@export If my number is revealed to trace a malicious call, will my data be stored and made available (Art 10(a))?
GIVEN `my provider overrode the hiding of my number to trace a malicious call` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the provider override the elimination of calling line identification under Art 10(a)?
      `the storing is in accordance with national law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the storing and making available in accordance with national law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If my number is revealed to trace a malicious call will my data be stored and made available` IS
    `Art 10(a) second sentence the data identifying the calling subscriber will be stored and made available by the provider` WITH
        `the provider has overridden the elimination of calling line identification under paragraph (a)` IS `my provider overrode the hiding of my number to trace a malicious call`
        `the storing and making available is in accordance with national law` IS `the storing is in accordance with national law`

@export I am a company: must my legitimate interests about my directory entry be protected (Art 12(4))?
GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a company must my legitimate interests about my directory entry be protected` IS
    `Art 12(4) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to their entry in public directories are sufficiently protected` WITH
        `the subscriber is a natural person` IS `I am a natural person`

@export Does the directory rule reach a directory edition that was already printed (Art 16(1))?
GIVEN `the edition was already produced or placed on the market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the edition already produced or placed on the market?
      `it is in printed or off-line electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in printed or off-line electronic form?
      `that was before the national law took effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that before the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive entered into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the directory rule reach a directory edition that was already printed` IS
    `Art 16(1) Article 12 applies to the edition of the directory` WITH
        `the edition was already produced or placed on the market` IS `the edition was already produced or placed on the market`
        `the edition is in printed or off-line electronic form` IS `it is in printed or off-line electronic form`
        `that was before the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive entered into force` IS `that was before the national law took effect`

§§ `My bill and my line identification (Articles 7 and 8)`

@export Do I have the right to a non-itemised bill (Art 7(1))?
GIVEN `I am a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subscriber (the person who has the contract with the provider)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the right to a non-itemised bill` IS
    `Art 7(1) the subscriber has the right to receive non-itemised bills` WITH
        `the person is a subscriber` IS `I am a subscriber`

@export Has my provider given me the possibility of hiding my number on a call I make (Art 8(1))?
GIVEN `my provider lets me hide my number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your provider let you prevent your number being shown to the person you call?
      `I can do it call by call` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you do it on a per-call basis?
      `it is simple to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my provider given me the possibility of hiding my number on a call I make` IS
    `Art 8(1) first sentence the service provider's duty to the calling user is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` IS `my provider lets me hide my number`
        `the possibility is on a per-call basis` IS `I can do it call by call`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple to do`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

@export When I am called, has my provider given me the possibility of hiding the caller's number from me (Art 8(2))?
GIVEN `my provider lets me stop callers' numbers being shown to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your provider let you prevent the number of incoming callers being shown to you?
      `it is simple to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by a simple means?
      `my use of this is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your use of this function reasonable?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my provider let me stop callers' numbers being shown to me` IS
    `Art 8(2) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls` IS `my provider lets me stop callers' numbers being shown to me`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple to do`
        `the use of this function is reasonable` IS `my use of this is reasonable`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

@export Can I reject calls whose caller has hidden their number (Art 8(3))?
GIVEN `my provider lets me reject calls from hidden numbers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your provider let you reject incoming calls where the caller has prevented the presentation of their number?
      `it is simple to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by a simple means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I reject incoming calls whose caller has hidden their number` IS
    `Art 8(3) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls where the presentation of the calling line identification has been prevented by the calling user or subscriber` IS `my provider lets me reject calls from hidden numbers`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple to do`

@export Can I stop my number being shown to the person who calls me when I answer (Art 8(4))?
GIVEN `my provider lets me hide who answers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your provider let you prevent the identity of the line that answers being shown to the caller?
      `it is simple to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I stop my connected line identification being shown to the caller` IS
    `Art 8(4) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the calling user` IS `my provider lets me hide who answers`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple to do`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

@export Does my right to hide my number also reach a call I make to another country (Art 8(5))?
GIVEN `the call is to a country outside the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the call to a country outside the Community?
      `the call starts in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the call originate in the Community?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my right to hide my number reach a call to another country` IS
    `Art 8(5) first sentence paragraph 1 applies to the call` WITH
        `the call is to a third country` IS `the call is to a country outside the Community`
        `the call originates in the Community` IS `the call starts in the Community`

@export Do my rights as the person called also reach a call from another country (Art 8(5))?
GIVEN `it is a call coming in to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an incoming call?
      `the call starts outside the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the call originate in a country outside the Community?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my rights as the person called reach a call from another country` IS
    `Art 8(5) second sentence paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 apply to the call` WITH
        `the call is an incoming call` IS `it is a call coming in to me`
        `the call originates in a third country` IS `the call starts outside the Community`

§§ `Where my phone is (Article 9)`
-- Only for a person whose location data is being processed by a provider or a value added service.

@export May my location data (other than traffic data) be processed (Art 9(1))?
GIVEN `it is location data about me held by a public network or service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it location data other than traffic data, about you as a user or subscriber of a public network or service?
      `it has been made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the data been made anonymous?
      `I consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent?
      `the processing is limited to what the value added service needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing to the extent and for the duration necessary to provide a value added service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my location data be processed` IS
    `Art 9(1) first sentence the location data may be processed` WITH
        `the data is location data other than traffic data, relating to users or subscribers of public communications networks or publicly available electronic communications services` IS `it is location data about me held by a public network or service`
        `the data is made anonymous` IS `it has been made anonymous`
        `the users or subscribers have consented` IS `I consented`
        `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for the provision of a value added service` IS `the processing is limited to what the value added service needs`

@export Has my provider told me what it must before asking my consent to location processing (Art 9(1))?
GIVEN `my provider told me what type of location data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your provider tell you the type of location data that will be processed?
      `my provider told me the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it tell you the purposes of the processing?
      `my provider told me how long` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it tell you the duration of the processing?
      `my provider told me whether a third party gets it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it tell you whether the data will be passed to a third party to provide the value added service?
      `my provider told me before I consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it tell you before you gave your consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my provider told me what it must before asking my consent to location processing` IS
    `Art 9(1) second sentence the service provider's duty to inform is met` WITH
        `the provider informed the users or subscribers of the type of location data other than traffic data which will be processed` IS `my provider told me what type of location data`
        `the provider informed them of the purposes of the processing` IS `my provider told me the purposes`
        `the provider informed them of the duration of the processing` IS `my provider told me how long`
        `the provider informed them whether the data will be transmitted to a third party for the purpose of providing the value added service` IS `my provider told me whether a third party gets it`
        `the provider did so prior to obtaining their consent` IS `my provider told me before I consented`

@export Can I withdraw my consent to location processing at any time (Art 9(1))?
GIVEN `I can withdraw my consent at any time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you withdraw your consent to the processing of your location data at any time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I withdraw my consent to location processing at any time` IS
    `Art 9(1) third sentence the possibility to withdraw the consent at any time is given` WITH
        `the users or subscribers have the possibility to withdraw their consent at any time` IS `I can withdraw my consent at any time`

@export Can I temporarily refuse the processing of my location for each connection (Art 9(2))?
GIVEN `I can temporarily refuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you temporarily refuse the processing of your location data?
      `it is simple to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it done by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
      `I can do it for each connection or each transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you do it for each connection to the network, or for each transmission of a communication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I temporarily refuse the processing of my location for each connection` IS
    `Art 9(2) the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing is as required` WITH
        `the user or subscriber has the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing of such data` IS `I can temporarily refuse`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple to do`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`
        `the possibility is for each connection to the network or for each transmission of a communication` IS `I can do it for each connection or each transmission`

§§ `Call forwarding and the directory (Articles 11 and 12)`

@export Must I be able to stop automatic call forwarding to my line (Art 11)?
GIVEN `I am a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subscriber?
      `calls are being forwarded to my line automatically by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a third party automatically forwarding calls to your terminal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be able to stop automatic call forwarding to my line` IS
    `Art 11 the subscriber must have the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding` WITH
        `the person is a subscriber` IS `I am a subscriber`
        `the forwarding is automatic call forwarding by a third party to the subscriber's terminal` IS `calls are being forwarded to my line automatically by a third party`

@export Must I be told about a directory before my details are put in it (Art 12(1))?
GIVEN `it is a printed or electronic directory open to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a printed or electronic directory of subscribers that is available to the public, or obtainable through directory enquiry services?
      `my details could be put in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could your personal data be included in it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be told about a directory before my details are put in it` IS
    `Art 12(1) the subscriber must be informed before inclusion in the directory` WITH
        `the directory is a printed or electronic directory of subscribers, available to the public or obtainable through directory enquiry services` IS `it is a printed or electronic directory open to the public`
        `the subscriber's personal data can be included in the directory` IS `my details could be put in it`

@export Was I told what I must be told, free of charge, before I was put in the directory (Art 12(1))?
GIVEN `I was told the purposes of the directory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you told the purpose or purposes of the directory?
      `the directory has search functions in an electronic version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directory have search functions built into an electronic version?
      `I was told what else those search functions allow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you told of the further uses that search functions allow?
      `I was told free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you told free of charge?
      `I was told before I was put in the directory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you told before you were included?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I told what I must be told before I was put in the directory` IS
    `Art 12(1) the subscriber's information before inclusion is as required` WITH
        `the subscriber was informed about the purpose or purposes of the directory` IS `I was told the purposes of the directory`
        `the directory has search functions embedded in an electronic version` IS `the directory has search functions in an electronic version`
        `the subscriber was informed of the further usage possibilities based on those search functions` IS `I was told what else those search functions allow`
        `the information was free of charge` IS `I was told free of charge`
        `the information was given before the subscriber was included in the directory` IS `I was told before I was put in the directory`

@export Must I be able to decide whether and what of mine is in a public directory and to correct or withdraw it (Art 12(2))?
GIVEN `it is a public directory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a public directory?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be able to decide what of mine is in a public directory` IS
    `Art 12(2) first sentence the subscriber must be given the opportunity to determine the inclusion of the personal data and to verify, correct or withdraw it` WITH
        `the directory is a public directory` IS `it is a public directory`

@export Is not being in a public directory, and checking, correcting or withdrawing my data, free of charge for me (Art 12(2))?
GIVEN `not being included was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was not being included in the directory free of charge?
      `verifying my data was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was verifying your data free of charge?
      `correcting my data was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was correcting your data free of charge?
      `withdrawing my data was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was withdrawing your data free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is not being in a public directory and correcting my data free of charge for me` IS
    `Art 12(2) second sentence the subscriber's non-inclusion, verifying, correcting and withdrawing are free of charge` WITH
        `not being included in the public subscriber directory was free of charge` IS `not being included was free`
        `verifying personal data was free of charge` IS `verifying my data was free`
        `correcting personal data was free of charge` IS `correcting my data was free`
        `withdrawing personal data from the directory was free of charge` IS `withdrawing my data was free`

@export Do the directory rights of paragraphs 1 and 2 reach me as a natural person (Art 12(4))?
GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the directory rights reach me as a natural person` IS
    `Art 12(4) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 2 apply to the subscriber` WITH
        `the subscriber is a natural person` IS `I am a natural person`

§§ `If my provider's network is attacked (Article 4)`
-- Only for a person whose provider has suffered, or is exposed to, a security problem.

@export Must my provider warn me of a particular risk to the security of the network (Art 4(2))?
GIVEN `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my provider warn me of a particular risk to the security of the network` IS
    `Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers concerning the risk` WITH
        `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network`

@export Must my provider also tell me about a personal data breach that may harm me (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `there has been a personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a personal data breach?
      `it is likely to harm my data or privacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely to adversely affect your personal data or privacy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my provider also tell me about a personal data breach that may harm me` IS
    `Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider must also notify the subscriber or individual` WITH
        `there has been a personal data breach` IS `there has been a personal data breach`
        `the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual` IS `it is likely to harm my data or privacy`

-- POLARITY SWAP: the layer-1 function asks "is notification to the subscriber or individual required?", and answers JUST FALSE where the text says it is not required (the provider is excused).
-- Here JUST TRUE = yes and JUST FALSE = no; the layer-1 function `Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` answers the opposite question, so its two definite answers are swapped in this DECIDE. NOTHING is left alone (NOTES.md, "Seat polarity audit").
@export Is my provider excused from telling me about the breach because it protected my data (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `my provider showed the authority it had protective measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your provider demonstrated to the competent authority's satisfaction that it had appropriate technological protection measures?
      `those measures covered my data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those measures applied to the data affected by the breach?
      `they make my data unintelligible to anyone not authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those measures render the data unintelligible to anyone not authorised to access it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my provider excused from telling me about the breach because it protected my data` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS `my provider showed the authority it had protective measures`, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS `those measures covered my data`, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS `they make my data unintelligible to anyone not authorised`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS `my provider showed the authority it had protective measures`, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS `those measures covered my data`, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS `they make my data unintelligible to anyone not authorised`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export Does the notice I was sent about the breach say what it must (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `it describes the nature of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice describe the nature of the personal data breach?
      `it gives contact points` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the contact points where I can get more information?
      `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it recommend measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the breach notice I was sent say what it must` IS
    `Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual has the content required` WITH
        `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS `it describes the nature of the breach`
        `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS `it gives contact points`
        `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS `it recommends measures to limit the harm`

§§ `Unsolicited messages and calls: the recipient (Article 13)`

-- The whole-Article answer, put together in layer 1 from paragraphs 1 to 5. JUST TRUE = the message may be sent; JUST FALSE = the text says it may not; NOTHING = the text does not answer.
@export May this marketing message be sent to me (Art 13)?
GIVEN `the message reached me by` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How did the message reach you? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `the message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `I did not ask for the message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message unsolicited (you did not ask for it)?
      `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
      `I gave my consent beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your consent before the message was sent?
      `the sender got my details from me as its customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sender obtain your electronic contact details from you as its customer?
      `I gave them when buying a product or service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give them in the context of the sale of a product or a service?
      `I gave them lawfully under Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
      `the sender is the business I bought from` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sender the same person (business) that obtained the details from you?
      `the message sells the sender's own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message about the sender's own products or services?
      `the products or services are similar to what I bought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products or services similar to those you bought?
      `I was clearly and distinctly offered a way to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object to this use of your details?
      `the offer to object was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that opportunity free of charge?
      `the offer to object was easy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it easy to use?
      `I was offered it when the details were collected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it offered when the details were collected?
      `I refused at the start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse such use at the start?
      `I was offered it with every message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you offered it on the occasion of each message?
      `the sender's identity is disguised or concealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message disguise or conceal the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent?
      `the message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message contravene Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC (the rules for commercial communications)?
      `there is no valid address to ask them to stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message have no valid address to which you can send a request that such messages cease?
      `the message pushes me to a website that breaks that Article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message encourage you to visit websites that contravene that Article?
      `national law has chosen` IS A `Article 13(3) national option` @desc For a message that is not an automatic call, fax or e-mail: has national law chosen that such messages need your consent, or that people who do not wish to receive them are protected? One of: consent of the subscriber or user is required, subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected, national legislation has not been stated.
      `I do not wish to receive these messages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not wish to receive these messages?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this marketing message be sent to me` IS
    `Art 13 the message may be sent to the recipient` WITH
        `means` IS `the message reached me by`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for direct marketing`
        `the message is unsolicited` IS `I did not ask for the message`
        `the recipient is a natural person` IS `I am a natural person`
        `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS `I gave my consent beforehand`
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `the sender got my details from me as its customer`
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `I gave them when buying a product or service`
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `I gave them lawfully under Directive 95/46/EC`
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `the sender is the business I bought from`
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `the message sells the sender's own products or services`
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `the products or services are similar to what I bought`
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `I was clearly and distinctly offered a way to object`
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the offer to object was free`
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the offer to object was easy`
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `I was offered it when the details were collected`
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS `I refused at the start`
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `I was offered it with every message`
        `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS `the sender's identity is disguised or concealed`
        `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS `the message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC`
        `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS `there is no valid address to ask them to stop`
        `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS `the message pushes me to a website that breaks that Article`
        `option` IS `national law has chosen`
        `the recipient does not wish to receive these communications` IS `I do not wish to receive these messages`

@export Is this use of the means allowed in respect of me because I gave my prior consent (Art 13(1))?
GIVEN `the message reached me by` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How did the message reach you? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `the message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `I gave my consent beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your consent before the message was sent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this use of the means allowed in respect of me because I gave my prior consent` IS
    `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` WITH
        `means` IS `the message reached me by`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for direct marketing`
        `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS `I gave my consent beforehand`

@export Can the sender rely on the existing-customer exception against me (Art 13(2))?
GIVEN `the message reached me by` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How did the message reach you? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `the sender got my details from me as its customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sender obtain your electronic contact details from you as its customer?
      `I gave them when buying a product or service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give them in the context of the sale of a product or a service?
      `I gave them lawfully under Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
      `the sender is the business I bought from` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sender the same person (business) that obtained the details from you?
      `the message sells the sender's own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message about the sender's own products or services?
      `the products or services are similar to what I bought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products or services similar to those you bought?
      `I was clearly and distinctly offered a way to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object to this use of your details?
      `the offer to object was free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that opportunity free of charge?
      `the offer to object was easy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it easy to use?
      `I was offered it when the details were collected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it offered when the details were collected?
      `I refused at the start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse such use at the start?
      `I was offered it with every message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you offered it on the occasion of each message?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the sender rely on the existing customer exception against me` IS
    `Art 13(2) the soft opt-in applies` WITH
        `means` IS `the message reached me by`
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `the sender got my details from me as its customer`
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `I gave them when buying a product or service`
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `I gave them lawfully under Directive 95/46/EC`
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `the sender is the business I bought from`
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `the message sells the sender's own products or services`
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `the products or services are similar to what I bought`
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `I was clearly and distinctly offered a way to object`
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the offer to object was free`
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the offer to object was easy`
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `I was offered it when the details were collected`
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS `I refused at the start`
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `I was offered it with every message`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the national law to make it not allowed. JUST FALSE is not reachable here; NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Must national law make an unsolicited marketing call or message that is not an automatic call, fax or e-mail not allowed (Art 13(3))?
GIVEN `the call or message reached me by` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How did it reach you? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `I did not ask for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it unsolicited (you did not ask for it)?
      `it is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `national law has chosen` IS A `Article 13(3) national option` @desc Has national law chosen that such communications need your consent, or that people who do not wish to receive them are protected? One of: consent of the subscriber or user is required, subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected, national legislation has not been stated.
      `I gave my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent to it?
      `I do not wish to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not wish to receive these communications?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must national law make an unsolicited marketing call that is not an automatic call fax or e-mail not allowed` IS
    `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` WITH
        `means` IS `the call or message reached me by`
        `the communication is unsolicited` IS `I did not ask for it`
        `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `it is for direct marketing`
        `option` IS `national law has chosen`
        `the subscriber or user has consented` IS `I gave my consent`
        `the subscriber or user does not wish to receive these communications` IS `I do not wish to receive them`

@export Is the option national law chose for such calls free of charge for me, as Art 13(3) requires?
GIVEN `the option is free of charge for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the option national law chose free of charge for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national option for such calls free of charge for me as Article 13(3) requires` IS
    `Art 13(3) the option is free of charge for the subscriber or user` WITH
        `the option the national legislation chose is free of charge for the subscriber or user` IS `the option is free of charge for me`

@export Is the practice of sending me this e-mail prohibited in any event (Art 13(4))?
GIVEN `the message reached me by` IS A `Marketing means` @desc How did the message reach you? One of: an automated calling and communication system without human intervention, a facsimile machine, an electronic mail message, another means of communication.
      `the message is for direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the message for the purposes of direct marketing?
      `the sender's identity is disguised or concealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message disguise or conceal the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent?
      `the message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message contravene Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC?
      `there is no valid address to ask them to stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message have no valid address to which you can send a request that such messages cease?
      `the message pushes me to a website that breaks that Article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the message encourage you to visit websites that contravene that Article?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the practice of sending me this e-mail prohibited in any event` IS
    `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` WITH
        `means` IS `the message reached me by`
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for direct marketing`
        `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS `the sender's identity is disguised or concealed`
        `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS `the message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC`
        `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS `there is no valid address to ask them to stop`
        `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS `the message pushes me to a website that breaks that Article`

@export As a natural person, do paragraphs 1 and 3 protect me (Art 13(5))?
GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a natural person do the marketing rules of paragraphs 1 and 3 protect me` IS
    `Art 13(5) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to the subscriber` WITH
        `the subscriber is a natural person` IS `I am a natural person`

@export I am a company: must my legitimate interests about unsolicited messages be sufficiently protected (Art 13(5))?
GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person (an individual rather than a company)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a company must my legitimate interests about unsolicited messages be protected` IS
    `Art 13(5) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to unsolicited communications are sufficiently protected` WITH
        `the subscriber is a natural person` IS `I am a natural person`

@export May I bring legal proceedings over an infringement of the national rules on these messages (Art 13(6))?
GIVEN `I am adversely affected by the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you adversely affected by an infringement of the national provisions adopted under Article 13?
      `I have a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement?
      `I am an electronic communications service provider protecting my business interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring legal proceedings over an infringement of the national rules on these messages` IS
    `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` WITH
        `the person is adversely affected by an infringement of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13` IS `I am adversely affected by the infringement`
        `the person has a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement` IS `I have a legitimate interest in stopping it`
        `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests` IS `I am an electronic communications service provider protecting my business interests`

@export If I go to court, does an administrative remedy still stand (Art 13(6))?
GIVEN `national law provides an administrative remedy under Art 15a(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does national law provide an administrative remedy (for example an order from the authority to stop) under Article 15a(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If I go to court does an administrative remedy still stand` IS
    `Art 13(6) the legal proceedings leave the administrative remedy unaffected` WITH
        `there is an administrative remedy for which provision is made under Article 15a(2)` IS `national law provides an administrative remedy under Art 15a(2)`

§§ `Remedies, penalties and enforcement (Articles 15, 15a and 16)`

@export Do the judicial remedies and sanctions of Directive 95/46/EC apply to my rights under this Directive (Art 15(2))?
GIVEN `it concerns national provisions adopted under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter concern national provisions adopted under this Directive?
      `it concerns a right I have under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern an individual right derived from this Directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the judicial remedies of Directive 95 46 EC apply to my rights under this Directive` IS
    `Art 15(2) Chapter III of Directive 95/46/EC on judicial remedies, liability and sanctions applies` WITH
        `the matter concerns national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive` IS `it concerns national provisions adopted under this Directive`
        `the matter concerns an individual right derived from this Directive` IS `it concerns a right I have under this Directive`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the Member State to give the body that power. JUST FALSE = no (another national body for which it is not relevant, "where relevant"). NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order this infringement to stop (Art 15a(2))?
GIVEN `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an infringement of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive?
      `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the competent national authority?
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body another national body?
      `it is relevant for that other body to have the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant that the other national body have the power?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order this infringement to stop` IS
    `Art 15a(2) the body must have the power to order the cessation of the infringement` WITH
        `the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive`
        `the body is the competent national authority` IS `the body is the competent national authority`
        `the body is another national body` IS `the body is another national body`
        `it is relevant that the other national body have the power` IS `it is relevant for that other body to have the power`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the Member State to give the body that power. JUST FALSE = no (another national body for which it is not relevant, "where relevant"). NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the powers to find out what it needs about this infringement (Art 15a(3))?
GIVEN `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the competent national authority?
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body another national body?
      `it is relevant for that other body to have the powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the powers to find out what it needs about this infringement` IS
    `Art 15a(3) the body must have the investigative powers and resources, including the power to obtain information` WITH
        `the body is the competent national authority` IS `the body is the competent national authority`
        `the body is another national body` IS `the body is another national body`
        `it is relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources` IS `it is relevant for that other body to have the powers`

@export May my Member State restrict my rights under this Directive for national security or crime (Art 15(1))?
GIVEN `the measure is a law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure a legislative measure?
      `the right is one of those listed` IS A `Restrictable provision` @desc Which right is restricted? One of: Article 5, Article 6, Article 8(1), Article 8(2), Article 8(3), Article 8(4), Article 9, another provision of this Directive.
      `the purpose` IS A `Restriction purpose` @desc What is the purpose? One of: national security (State security), defence, public security, the prevention, investigation, detection and prosecution of criminal offences or of unauthorised use of the electronic communication system, another purpose.
      `the restriction is necessary, appropriate and proportionate in a democratic society` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the restriction a necessary, appropriate and proportionate measure within a democratic society?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my Member State restrict my rights for national security or crime` IS
    `Art 15(1) first sentence the Member State may adopt the legislative measure restricting the scope of the rights and obligations` WITH
        `the measure is a legislative measure` IS `the measure is a law`
        `provision` IS `the right is one of those listed`
        `purpose` IS `the purpose`
        `the restriction constitutes a necessary, appropriate and proportionate measure within a democratic society` IS `the restriction is necessary, appropriate and proportionate in a democratic society`

-- Checked on 2026-11-17 against the Publications Office data (the judgment's relation to the Directive only, not its effect on this paragraph): the Court of Justice declared Directive 2006/24/EC void by preliminary ruling on 8 April 2014 (CELEX 62012CJ0293), so this paragraph's reference may no longer have effect. The paragraph is encoded as printed (NOTES.md, fork register).
@export Does Article 15(1) apply to data that another Directive requires my provider to retain (Art 15(1a))?
GIVEN `the data is required to be retained by Directive 2006/24/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data specifically required by Directive 2006/24/EC to be retained?
      `it is retained for the purposes in Article 1(1) of that Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to be retained for the purposes referred to in Article 1(1) of that Directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Article 15(1) apply to data that another Directive requires to be retained` IS
    `Art 15(1a) paragraph 1 applies to the data` WITH
        `the data is specifically required by Directive 2006/24/EC to be retained` IS `the data is required to be retained by Directive 2006/24/EC`
        `it is to be retained for the purposes referred to in Article 1(1) of that Directive` IS `it is retained for the purposes in Article 1(1) of that Directive`

@export May my old directory entry stay in a public directory after the new law began (Art 16(2))?
GIVEN `I am a fixed or mobile voice telephony subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subscriber to a fixed or mobile public voice telephony service?
      `I was put in the directory lawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your data included in a public subscriber directory in conformity with Directive 95/46/EC and Article 11 of Directive 97/66/EC?
      `that was before the national law began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that before the national provisions adopted under this Directive came into force?
      `I said I want to be removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you indicated otherwise (that you want to be removed)?
      `I was given complete information about purposes and options` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received complete information about purposes and options in accordance with Article 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my old directory entry stay in a public directory after the new law began` IS
    `Art 16(2) the personal data of the subscriber may remain included in the public directory` WITH
        `the subscriber is a subscriber to a fixed or mobile public voice telephony service` IS `I am a fixed or mobile voice telephony subscriber`
        `the data was included in a public subscriber directory in conformity with Directive 95/46/EC and Article 11 of Directive 97/66/EC` IS `I was put in the directory lawfully`
        `that was before the national provisions adopted in pursuance of this Directive entered into force` IS `that was before the national law began`
        `the subscriber has indicated otherwise` IS `I said I want to be removed`
        `the subscriber has received complete information about purposes and options in accordance with Article 12` IS `I was given complete information about purposes and options`
